"In gymnastic competitions, such as the Olympics, gymnasts perform choreographed routines on the balance beam. Scores are calculated by several judges according to degree of difficulty, artistic merit and execution of the routine. This means that the more difficult and appealing the routine, it will receive higher scores than a simple routine as long as there are no mistakes. The judging system encourages gymnasts to push their limits and strive for perfection.": "ac43ac40c2eb",
